//@version=6
indicator("vw-w6-forin-fn-two-sites")

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-07 for the Pine parity programme from row W6-F1 of
// docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-06-w6-t6.md, whose shapes are W6-BREAKDOWN.md section 6's W6-F1 row
// (branch docs/pine-w6-breakdown): "`for ... in` inside a UDF at two call sites over different arrays".
// One shape of W6-F1 per file. No licence-held text.
// NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW: a line that does not compile IS a reading - record the error text and the line.
// QUESTION: a user function whose body walks its parameter with `for ... in`, called at two sites over two
// different arrays: does each call walk its own array (U01 = open + close, U02 = high + low + close)?
// Our runtime lane refuses it by name: "inside a function body, ..." (W6-F1). A00 is the control.
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D, inputs at defaults.

total(array<float> a) =>
    float s = 0.0
    for x in a
        s += x
    s

plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
a1 = array.from(open, close)
a2 = array.from(high, low, close)

plot(total(a1), "U01_site1_sum")
plot(total(a2), "U02_site2_sum")
